            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Missing Context       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.32.0], [1.16.0]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 0.32.0 and 1.16.0, Axios’s Node.js HTTP adapter may forward a Proxy-Authorization header to a redirected origin during specific proxy-to-direct redirect flows. This affects Node.js usage, where an initial HTTP request is sent through an authenticated HTTP proxy, redirects are followed, and the redirected URL is no longer proxied. Under affected redirect shapes, the final origin can receive the proxy credential that was intended only for the outbound proxy. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.32.0 and 1.16.0."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Missing Context       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.32.0], [1.16.0]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 0.32.0 and 1.16.0, Axios’s Node.js HTTP adapter may forward a Proxy-Authorization header to a redirected origin during specific proxy-to-direct redirect flows. This affects Node.js usage, where an initial HTTP request is sent through an authenticated HTTP proxy, redirects are followed, and the redirected URL is no longer proxied. Under affected redirect shapes, the final origin can receive the proxy credential that was intended only for the outbound proxy. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.32.0 and 1.16.0."
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-44487_axios_0.18.0",
              "name": "CVE-2026-44487-axios-0.18.0",
              "properties": {
                "impactPaths": [
                  [
                    {
                      "id": "npm://user-management-service:1.0.0",
                      "name": "user-management-service",
                      "version": "1.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://axios:0.18.0",
                      "name": "axios",
                      "version": "0.18.0"
                    }
                  ]
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[CVE-2026-44487] axios 0.18.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Missing Context       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.31.1], [1.15.1]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, he fix for no_proxy hostname normalization bypass is incomplete. When no_proxy=localhost is set, requests to 127.0.0.1 and [::1] still route through the proxy instead of bypassing it. The shouldBypassProxy() function does pure string matching — it does not resolve IP aliases or loopback equivalents. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Missing Context       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.31.1], [1.15.1]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, he fix for no_proxy hostname normalization bypass is incomplete. When no_proxy=localhost is set, requests to 127.0.0.1 and [::1] still route through the proxy instead of bypassing it. The shouldBypassProxy() function does pure string matching — it does not resolve IP aliases or loopback equivalents. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1."
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-42038_axios_0.18.0",
              "name": "CVE-2026-42038-axios-0.18.0",
