            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 5.3      | Not Covered       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.31.1], [1.15.1]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, for stream request bodies, maxBodyLength is bypassed when maxRedirects is set to 0 (native http/https transport path). Oversized streamed uploads are sent fully even when the caller sets strict body limits. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1."
              },
              "help": {
