              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[CVE-2026-93687] braces 3.0.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 5.4      | Not Covered       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [1.1.4]   |",
                "text": "Incorrect parsing of certain JSON input may result in js-bson not correctly serializing BSON. This may cause unexpected application behaviour including data disclosure. This issue affects: MongoDB Inc. js-bson library version 1.1.3 and prior to."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 5.4      | Not Covered       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [1.1.4]   |",
                "text": "Incorrect parsing of certain JSON input may result in js-bson not correctly serializing BSON. This may cause unexpected application behaviour including data disclosure. This issue affects: MongoDB Inc. js-bson library version 1.1.3 and prior to."
              },
              "id": "CVE-2019-2391_bson_1.0.9",
              "name": "CVE-2019-2391-bson-1.0.9",
              "properties": {
                "impactPaths": [
                  [
                    {
                      "id": "npm://user-management-service:1.0.0",
                      "name": "user-management-service",
                      "version": "1.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://mongoose:5.0.0",
                      "name": "mongoose",
                      "version": "5.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://bson:1.0.9",
                      "name": "bson",
                      "version": "1.0.9"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "id": "npm://user-management-service:1.0.0",
                      "name": "user-management-service",
                      "version": "1.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://mongoose:5.0.0",
                      "name": "mongoose",
                      "version": "5.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://mongodb:3.0.1",
                      "name": "mongodb",
                      "version": "3.0.1"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://mongodb-core:3.0.1",
                      "name": "mongodb-core",
                      "version": "3.0.1"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://bson:1.0.9",
                      "name": "bson",
                      "version": "1.0.9"
                    }
                  ]
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.4"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[CVE-2019-2391] bson 1.0.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 6.5      | Not Covered       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [6.13.10], [7.8.10], [8.24.1], [9.7.2]   |",
                "text": "Mongoose is a MongoDB object modeling tool designed to work in an asynchronous environment. Prior to 6.13.10, 7.8.10, 8.24.1, and 9.7.2, passing a user-controlled update such as MyModel.updateOne(filter, req.body) can exploit Mongoose update casting with a __proto__.x dotted path under $set. Schema.prototype.path and Schema.prototype._getPathType can treat inherited properties of schema.paths and schema.nested as schema types, allowing the casting process to set $fullPath and $parentSchemaDocArray on Object.prototype before throwing. This prototype pollution makes those properties visible on newly created objects and can cause application integrity and availability impacts. This issue is fixed in versions 6.13.10, 7.8.10, 8.24.1, and 9.7.2."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 6.5      | Not Covered       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [6.13.10], [7.8.10], [8.24.1], [9.7.2]   |",
                "text": "Mongoose is a MongoDB object modeling tool designed to work in an asynchronous environment. Prior to 6.13.10, 7.8.10, 8.24.1, and 9.7.2, passing a user-controlled update such as MyModel.updateOne(filter, req.body) can exploit Mongoose update casting with a __proto__.x dotted path under $set. Schema.prototype.path and Schema.prototype._getPathType can treat inherited properties of schema.paths and schema.nested as schema types, allowing the casting process to set $fullPath and $parentSchemaDocArray on Object.prototype before throwing. This prototype pollution makes those properties visible on newly created objects and can cause application integrity and availability impacts. This issue is fixed in versions 6.13.10, 7.8.10, 8.24.1, and 9.7.2."
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-73562_mongoose_5.0.0",
              "name": "CVE-2026-73562-mongoose-5.0.0",
              "properties": {
                "impactPaths": [
                  [
                    {
                      "id": "npm://user-management-service:1.0.0",
                      "name": "user-management-service",
                      "version": "1.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://mongoose:5.0.0",
                      "name": "mongoose",
                      "version": "5.0.0"
                    }
                  ]
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[CVE-2026-73562] mongoose 5.0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Not Applicable       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.32.0], [1.16.0]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Axios versions before 0.32.0 on the 0.x line and before 1.16.0 on the 1.x line build a regular expression from the configured XSRF cookie name without escaping regex metacharacters. In standard browser environments, an attacker who can influence the cookie name passed to axios can cause expensive regex backtracking while axios reads document.cookie. The practical impact is client-side availability degradation, such as freezing the affected browser tab while axios prepares a request. The issue does not affect ordinary Node.js HTTP adapter usage, React Native, or web workers, where axios does not read document.cookie. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.32.0 and 1.16.0."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 7.5      | Not Applicable       | `axios 0.18.0`       | [0.32.0], [1.16.0]   |",
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Axios versions before 0.32.0 on the 0.x line and before 1.16.0 on the 1.x line build a regular expression from the configured XSRF cookie name without escaping regex metacharacters. In standard browser environments, an attacker who can influence the cookie name passed to axios can cause expensive regex backtracking while axios reads document.cookie. The practical impact is client-side availability degradation, such as freezing the affected browser tab while axios prepares a request. The issue does not affect ordinary Node.js HTTP adapter usage, React Native, or web workers, where axios does not read document.cookie. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.32.0 and 1.16.0."
              },
              "id": "CVE-2026-44496_axios_0.18.0",
              "name": "CVE-2026-44496-axios-0.18.0",
              "properties": {
                "impactPaths": [
                  [
                    {
                      "id": "npm://user-management-service:1.0.0",
                      "name": "user-management-service",
                      "version": "1.0.0"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "npm://axios:0.18.0",
                      "name": "axios",
                      "version": "0.18.0"
                    }
                  ]
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "[CVE-2026-44496] axios 0.18.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 9.1      | Not Applicable       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [4.13.21], [5.7.5]   |",
                "text": "Automattic Mongoose through 5.7.4 allows attackers to bypass access control (in some applications) because any query object with a _bsontype attribute is ignored. For example, adding \"_bsontype\":\"a\" can sometimes interfere with a query filter. NOTE: this CVE is about Mongoose's failure to work around this _bsontype special case that exists in older versions of the bson parser (aka the mongodb/js-bson project)."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "| Severity Score | Contextual Analysis | Direct Dependencies | Fixed Versions     |\n|  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |  :---:  |\n| 9.1      | Not Applicable       | `mongoose 5.0.0`       | [4.13.21], [5.7.5]   |",
                "text": "Automattic Mongoose through 5.7.4 allows attackers to bypass access control (in some applications) because any query object with a _bsontype attribute is ignored. For example, adding \"_bsontype\":\"a\" can sometimes interfere with a query filter. NOTE: this CVE is about Mongoose's failure to work around this _bsontype special case that exists in older versions of the bson parser (aka the mongodb/js-bson project)."
              },
